---
import UrlForm from '../components/UrlForm.astro';

const title = 'WordPress to Astro in minutes | Exodus by DeployHQ';
const description =
	'Paste your WordPress URL. Exodus rebuilds your site as a static Astro project and deploys a live preview on DeployHQ.';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>{title}</title>
		<meta name="description" content={description} />
		<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
		<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<main>
			<section class="hero" id="preview">
				<h1>See your WordPress site running on Astro in minutes.</h1>
				<p class="subhead">
					Paste your URL. Exodus rebuilds your site as a static Astro project and deploys a live
					preview on DeployHQ.
				</p>
				<UrlForm id="url-hero" />
				<p class="microcopy">Free. Takes a few minutes. Your WordPress site isn't touched.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>The problem</h2>
				<p>
					Updates, plugin conflicts, security patches, and a server to keep it all alive, for a site
					whose content changes a couple of times a year. Moving to a static site fixes that, but
					doing it by hand means exporting content, rebuilding templates and re-checking every
					page. For a client portfolio, that's months of work.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>How it works</h2>
				<ol>
					<li>
						<strong>Paste your URL.</strong> Exodus reads your public site: pages, posts, images and
						metadata. Nothing gets installed on WordPress.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>We build an Astro project.</strong> Static pages with your content.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Open your live link.</strong> Your site is deployed on DeployHQ. Compare it with
						the original, check the speed score, or send the link to a client.
					</li>
				</ol>
				<p><a class="cta" href="#preview">Build my preview</a></p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>What converts, and what doesn't</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Converts:</strong> pages, posts, images, menus, metadata.</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Needs a replacement:</strong> forms, site search, comments, WooCommerce,
						memberships and plugin-driven features.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>Exodus lists what it found, so you know before you commit to anything.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Why Astro</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Static HTML: no PHP and no database, so there's nothing to patch.</li>
					<li>JavaScript only where a page needs it, which usually means faster pages.</li>
					<li>Content lives as files, so people and AI coding agents can edit it.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>This is a preview, not a migration</h2>
				<p>Your WordPress site stays exactly as it is.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="closing">
				<h2>Paste a URL. See what you'd get.</h2>
				<UrlForm id="url-closing" />
			</section>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>

<style is:global>
	:root {
		color-scheme: light dark;
		--bg: #ffffff;
		--fg: #1a1a1a;
		--muted: #5b5b5b;
		--accent: #5b3df5;
		--accent-fg: #ffffff;
		--border: #d4d4d8;
	}

	@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
		:root {
			--bg: #101014;
			--fg: #f2f2f4;
			--muted: #a1a1aa;
			--accent: #8b74ff;
			--accent-fg: #101014;
			--border: #3a3a44;
		}
	}

	* {
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	body {
		margin: 0;
		background: var(--bg);
		color: var(--fg);
		font: 1.0625rem/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
	}

	main {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 0 1rem 4rem;
	}

	section {
		padding: 2.5rem 0 0;
	}

	.hero {
		padding-top: 4rem;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3rem);
		line-height: 1.15;
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	h2 {
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		line-height: 1.25;
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
	}

	.subhead {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
	}

	.microcopy {
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
	}

	.url-form {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.5rem;
	}

	.url-form input {
		flex: 1 1 16rem;
		min-width: 0;
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		font: inherit;
		color: inherit;
		background: transparent;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
	}

	.url-form input[aria-invalid='true'] {
		border-color: #dc2626;
	}

	.url-form button,
	.cta {
		padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
		font: inherit;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--accent-fg);
		background: var(--accent);
		border: 0;
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		cursor: pointer;
		text-decoration: none;
		display: inline-block;
	}

	.url-form button:hover,
	.cta:hover {
		filter: brightness(1.1);
	}

	:focus-visible {
		outline: 3px solid var(--accent);
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}

	.url-form-status {
		flex-basis: 100%;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
	}

	.visually-hidden {
		position: absolute;
		width: 1px;
		height: 1px;
		margin: -1px;
		overflow: hidden;
		clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
		white-space: nowrap;
	}

	li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
</style>
